<!-- 
  Per-layer offset support:
  =========================
  You can specify a different x_offset for each layer using the x_offsets attribute.
  This is a comma-separated list of values with units:
  
  Example: x_offsets="0*cm, 1*cm, -0.5*cm, 2*mm, 0*cm"
  
  - The offsets are applied in order to each layer of that type (wide or thin)
  - If fewer offsets than layers, the list cycles (wraps around)
  - Supports units: cm, mm, m
  - Supports negative values for opposite direction offsets
  
  For backward compatibility, you can still use the single x_offset="0*cm" attribute,
  which applies the same offset to all layers.

  Per-layer extrazgap support:
  ============================
  You can specify a different gap after each layer using extrazgaps attribute.
  This is a comma-separated list of values with units:
  
  Example: extrazgaps="0*mm, 4*mm, 0*mm, 4*mm, ..."
  
  The extrazgaps attribute is now supported on THREE element types:
  
  1. <passive_layer extrazgaps="...">  - Gap AFTER each passive layer (code '7')
  2. <thinbar extrazgaps="...">        - Gap AFTER each thin bar layer (code '3' or '4')
  3. <widebar extrazgaps="...">        - Gap AFTER each wide bar layer (code '1' or '2')
  
  - The gaps are applied in order after each layer of that type
  - If fewer gaps than layers, the list cycles (wraps around)
  - Supports units: cm, mm, m
  
  For backward compatibility, you can still use the single extrazgap="0.5*cm" attribute,
  which applies the same gap after all layers of that type.
-->

